    "answer": {
      "state": "completed",
      "text": "Outcome: resolve_environment. The loan is not ready to ship.\n\nThe borrower's gallery is recorded at 80°F and 70% relative humidity. That is well above the usual museum loan conditions of about 70°F and roughly 50% RH. High heat and humidity together put objects at risk of mold, corrosion and dimensional change. One summary says the review found no environmental issues, but the actual readings contradict it, so the environment needs to be fixed before shipment. Clara Meyer's institution should bring the gallery into standard conditions and document stable readings, with Andrei Rossi confirming.\n\nThe other areas look acceptable on the evidence we have:\n- **Security:** the facility has 24-hour physical security.\n- **Light:** readings peak at 15 footcandles at the case, with no daylight reaching it. This should be rechecked if the objects are light-sensitive, because the object type isn't recorded.\n- **Off-gassing:** new materials will have off-gassed for 42 days before installation.\n- **Insurance:** the loan is covered by Smithsonian insurance at the borrower's expense, as the loan agreement requires.\n- **Handling:** experienced professional staff will handle, pack and transport the objects.",
